{{- /* index.tmpl is web/src/pages/index.astro. Whitespace in this file is output: the published build emits the
       markup with no whitespace between tags, so keep it on one line. */ -}}
{{- define "index" -}}<h1>Ranked statistics, published as static pages</h1><p>{{ if .Site.Live }}This site aggregates League of Legends ranked matches into per-patch tier lists and champion matchup tables, then pre-renders them.{{ else }}This site publishes per-patch tier lists and champion matchup tables, pre-rendered as static pages.{{ end }} There is no client-side data fetching and no JavaScript is required to read any page: what the HTML says is the whole product. {{ .IntroTail }}</p><h2>Current snapshot</h2>{{ if .Partition }}<ul><li>Patch <strong>{{ .Partition.Patch }}</strong> &middot; {{ .Partition.Region }} &middot; queue {{ .Partition.Queue }} &middot; bracket {{ .Partition.Bracket }}</li><li>Source window {{ windowLabel .Partition.SourceWindow.From .Partition.SourceWindow.To }}</li><li>Snapshot generated {{ utcStamp .Partition.GeneratedAt }}</li><li>{{ integer .Partition.CellsPublished }} published cells over {{ integer (len .Partition.Champions) }} champions; rates published from n = {{ integer .Partition.MinCellN }} games</li><li>{{ integer .Partition.SuppressedCells }} cells withheld for being below that threshold, and shown as withheld wherever they appear</li></ul>{{ else }}<div class="fallback-empty" role="note"><p><strong>No sample yet</strong></p><p>{{ .EmptyReason }}</p></div>{{ end }}<h2>Tier lists by role</h2><ul>{{ range .Roles }}<li><a href="/tier-list/{{ roleSlug . }}">{{ roleLabel . }} tier list</a> &middot; <a href="/matchups/{{ roleSlug . }}">{{ roleLabel . }} matchups</a></li>{{ end }}</ul><h2>{{ if .Site.Live }}How to read these numbers{{ else }}How these numbers will be read{{ end }}</h2>{{ if not .Site.Live }}<p>{{ if .Site.Demo }}The conventions below are the ones this build already renders, but the sample sizes and rates behind them are illustrative demo values rather than measured games.{{ else }}This build publishes no sample sizes and no rates yet; the conventions below are the ones every page is laid out for.{{ end }}</p>{{ end }}<ul><li>Every win, pick and ban rate is shown with the number of games it was measured over.</li><li>A rate is published only where the cell holds at least {{ .Threshold }}; thinner cells are shown as withheld, with their count and no rate.</li><li>Each rate carries a 95% interval, because 52% over 900 games and 52% over 90,000 games are not the same claim.</li><li>{{ if .Site.Live }}Rank data comes from Riot&#39;s match feed, which does not attribute a match to the player&#39;s exact rank, so bracket figures are a snapshot attribution rather than a per-match one.{{ else }}Riot does not attribute a match to the player&#39;s exact rank, so on a published snapshot the bracket figures are a snapshot attribution rather than a per-match one.{{ end }}</li></ul><p><a href="/about">How these numbers are produced</a></p><h2>Champions</h2><p>{{ integer (len .Site.Champions) }} champions are known to this build from Data Dragon {{ .Site.DdragonVersion }}. Each has a page for every role it has been played in this snapshot.</p><ul class="fallback-champion-links">{{ range .Site.Champions }}<li><a href="/champions/{{ .Slug }}">{{ .Name }}</a></li>{{ end }}</ul>{{- end -}}
